  "description": "<img width=\"30%\" src=\"https://gtif-ukif.github.io/gtif-ukif-client/assets/EDA-logo.png\">\n\nTime series of the column of excess methane from waste in Greece. UNEP classifies this location as a persistent emitter of methane and we see a consistent excess of methane from about July 2023 to August 2023, along with a coincident EMIT and Sentinel-2 data showing excess methane emissions on July 23rd, 2023. The vertical dot-dashed lines correspond to detected methane plumes from the EMIT satellite.",
